    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363">

                <pb facs="0597" n="1183" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p2/pg1183"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">796.00/8–349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in the Philippines
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-04T18:00:00-04:00">August 4, 1949—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>928. Thus far ltr contained your 1889 Aug 3<anchor n="1" xml:id="d363-f1"/> has
                    recd little or no publicity this country. Obviously story under Wash dateline
                    wld carry implication US had brought this ltr to pass. Very important ltr
                    receive wide publicity both here and Asia. Suggest you get in touch immed with
                    Romulo so that he can take steps on his own initiative to ensure wide publicity.
                    No doubt he will already have had ltr sent to all Phil missions with suggestions
                    they give it to govts to which accredited and to press in those countries.
                    However, important that stories in Amer press shd be recd from Manila and
                    published under Manila dateline.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
